 "result": "maze.py is a level-by-level BFS over a padded bytearray grid with a sentinel border. It reads all of stdin, locates S and E, marks visited cells by overwriting them with '#', and returns the first-hit distance or -1. The four neighbour checks are unrolled. It passes all three samples (2008, -1, 78) and was registered by assay at baseline 4.03312 with noise 2.7%. I am resting rather than spending more energy on variants, since prior lineage attempts at micro-optimisation of this same structure gained little (+0 to +10%) and each mid-model step costs more than a likely win returns.",
